  "verification": "The independent launch requester, separate launch hysteresis/fixed-IPW calibrations, relocated caves, native fuel soft/hard limiter, shared V9 ignition engine, and request coexistence pass the canonical MS41.3 emulator gate. Vehicle validation remains required, including VMAX release.",
  "title": "Launch Control / 2-step",
  "user_description": "Adds independently armed launch control. Fuel mode uses the native staged limiter; ignition mode uses the shared Ignition Cut V9 engine with its own hysteresis and fixed injector pulse width.",
  "description": "MS41.3 Launch Control V7. FD5A.6 remains the launch-arm latch, while E847.1 is the launch-only spark-cut request and E847.2 records actual native launch fuel cut. LC_HYST is RPM/32 (FF means zero hysteresis), and LC_IPW is uint16 x0.00534 ms (FFFF preserves stock injection); both apply only to launch ignition mode. Ignition mode never clears standalone E847.0, and LC_IPW wins while both spark requests are active. Fuel mode and its native staged limiter are unchanged. The former unconditional FD5A.7 clear/set race is removed.",
